entire trail update — Update project intent and lifecycle

When to use this:
Trail commands talk to entire.io and read the saved login from the OS
keyring (the Keychain on macOS), so they need network and keyring access.
If you run commands in a sandbox, request unsandboxed execution for
`entire trail` up front. An error saying the Keychain is not accessible or
the network is not allowed means the sandbox blocked it, not that the user
is logged out: ask to re-run it unsandboxed, and do not run `entire login`.


Local follow-up: Repeat two hollow-dotted arcs with staggered gaps, followed by one full circle of short dashes. Rotate neighboring rings in opposite directions at different speeds, and keep them stationary under reduced motion.

Warden follow-up: Enlarge the Blackout hero eye and have the slit scan down toward Jev, touching both eyelids and growing taller and wider through the center. Keep the pupil centered and still under reduced motion.

